{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The step drill bits complement my rivets and threaded inserts because making appropriately sized holes is a practical next step in using those supplies.",
    "The screw assortment fits my repeated interest in fastener kits: several lengths give me useful options for repair and assembly without needing one exact project specification."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Both filament recommendations assume a printing need that my purchases do not establish; working with tools and fabrication supplies does not mean I own or currently use a 3D printer.",
    "The large screw eyes and pressure gauge serve specific hanging or pressure measurement tasks that I do not currently have, even though they could belong in a workshop."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat general workshop use as enough of a connection, when I care more about whether something supports the fastening and assembly work I am doing.",
    "My interest in screw assortments seems to have been extended to individual screw packs without enough attention to whether I need their particular length and thread."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My rivet, rivet nut, drill bit, and measuring tool purchases point toward supplies that work together for drilling and joining materials; that practical connection makes the step bits especially relevant.",
    "I already own several fastener assortments, so another pack needs to fill a specific gap. Thread compatibility, required length, and what I already have matter more than simply being another metric screw."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my fastening and fabrication interests but sometimes mistake broad workshop relevance for a concrete next project need."
}"}
